    {
      "text": "Then Indra decided to catch Ravana alive. His army surrounded the demon king. For the first time, Ravana was fighting only to escape. At that moment, Ravana's son Meghnad came into the battle. He knew he could not beat Indra in a fair fight, so he used magic to become invisible and attacked from where Indra could not see him. In the end, he defeated Indra and took him to Lanka as a prisoner. That is why Meghnad is called Indrajit, the one who won over Indra. It became so serious that Brahma himself came to Lanka and asked for Indra to be set free. So Ravana, who beat kings and gods, was saved from Indra by his own son, who then took Indra himself as a prisoner. Who do you think was stronger, Ravana or Indra?",
